Adminer on FenrirOS
===================

Installed inert: the files are /usr/share/adminer/adminer.php (all database
systems) and editor.php (Adminer Editor). There is no web server site, no
PHP pool and no account: Adminer signs in with a database server's own user
and password (and refuses an empty password).

The PHP extension of each database you want to reach must be installed
(mysqli for MySQL/MariaDB, pgsql / pdo_pgsql, sqlite3 / pdo_sqlite, ...).

To serve it, an example for nginx with php-fpm, limited to your own address
(never expose a database admin tool to the internet):

    location = /adminer.php {
        allow 192.168.0.0/16;
        deny all;
        root /usr/share/adminer;
        include fastcgi_params;
        fastcgi_param SCRIPT_FILENAME /usr/share/adminer/adminer.php;
        fastcgi_pass unix:/run/php-fpm.sock;
    }

or, for a quick local session without a web server:

    php -S 127.0.0.1:8080 -t /usr/share/adminer
    (then open http://127.0.0.1:8080/adminer.php)
